{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Reviewing Legal Aspects of Software License Agreements"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when talking about software licenses. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Define strategies to make terms of reference and supplier assessment processes, in technology acquisition, based on established protocols. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive of Ought To"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> in <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span> to give suggestions in different situations."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Liability ought to be reduced with the proper provisions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ought to</span> is a modal verb that we can use to\u2026   <ul><li>express an opinion when something is right or wrong. </li>  <li>make predictions about something that is expected. <li>offer advice</li>. </li></ul><br/>  To use <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> in <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span>, you can follow the next grammatical structure: <br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">Ought to</span> + <span class=\"strong\">Be</span> + <span class=\"strong\">Verb in Past Participle</span> + Complement</div><br/>  Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Licenses <span class=\"strong\">ought to be checked</span> frequently. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Risks associated to data breach and how to solve them ought to be studied. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "For instance, cost ought to be analyzed. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Finally, sensitivity ought to be analyzed."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Scope of a Software License: Licensor and Licensee"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When analyzing the agreements of software licensing, two parts are involved: the licensor and the licensee."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Licensor's perspective</span>: You need a software licensing agreement in case you want to share your software with others while maintaining the ownership. You can limit how software is used and its purposes. Besides, a licensor can restrict the license with limits of the fields that are used, geographic restrictions, number of users allowed, hardware that is used, and ability to transfer the software. <br/><br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Licensee's perspective</span>: This person is in charge of negotiating the rights to use the software. He could get additional fees in case of exceeding the restrictions.  Therefore, it's important to consider possible future needs. Besides, the licensee has to negotiate the rights of the software in case competitors want to use it. <br/><br/>  When acquiring a software and negotiating the licensing agreement, both need to see all the details regarding the scope of the license."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "risk  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a situation that could possibly cause danger or negative consequences "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Risks associated to data breach and how to solve them ought to be studied."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "non-negotiable   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that doesn't take part of an agreement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some license agreements are non-negotiable, that's why they present little risk."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "suitable  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is appropriated for a specific case"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: And the potential licensee needs to consider if the vendor's agreement is appropriated and is suitable for the customer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "scope "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "possibility for something to be used"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The scope of the license must be expanded as necessary to cover the software needs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "off the hook "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when somebody is innocent "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: And what's more, in case of force majeure events, vendors are off the hook."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text",